-- Example data for the pages added on 2 October 2026, played through the system by the staff
-- whose job each step is (Emmanuel - finance, Aline - logistics, Eric - fleet, Nadine - warehouse):
--   * 3 suppliers: Tanzania Cross-Border Haulage, MSC Mediterranean Shipping (Rwanda), Rwanda Revenue Authority
--   * supplier bills: 1 part paid (USD), 1 fully paid (RWF + VAT), 1 garage bill in draft, 1 escort bill in draft
--   * disbursements: duty + port charges recharged at cost on a Kigali Hardware invoice (part paid),
--     an inspection fee for Virunga still to invoice, and container detention recharged to Virunga
--   * customer storage: Kigali Hardware nails (1,200 cartons, 2 gate passes, storage invoice in draft),
--     Akagera coffee (320 bags at Rubavu, still in its free days)
--   * containers: one returned in time, one on detention, one out on the journey below
--   * workshop: an in-house job card that used an oil drum from stock (approved), a tyre job at an outside garage
--   * journey Dar es Salaam -> Rusumo -> Kigali: leg 1 done and the cargo handed to leg 2, which is waiting
--   * bank reconciliation: this month's statement for the main bank account, matched, the bank fee posted
--
-- Import ONCE, after update_2026-10-02.sql. It needs the earlier sample data (Kigali Hardware, Virunga,
-- Akagera, RAD 482 K, RAE 219 C, the two warehouses, emmanuel/aline/eric/nadine@itec.rw).
-- Reference numbers continue from what the database already holds, so nothing clashes.
-- One transaction: if any line fails, nothing is saved. Importing it a second time is refused.
-- The example emails stay in the outbox for show, marked so they are never sent.

SET NAMES utf8mb4;
START TRANSACTION;

-- Refuses a second import: this row can only be added once.
